 "text": "Hi, how have you been? Honestly, yes, at some places. A good chef will keep your food hot, present it well, and take menu requests. Many menus list a quiet area, or you can ask at the table. Some restaurants even have a completely separate quiet kitchen. Then treat her to a proper meal out, not just a quick pasta. A seafood paella or a roast chicken with vegetables is much easier on the hearing. A typical chef's table is an hour or so, start to finish. Your mum will get to see the kitchen in action, then she can order something she knows she'll enjoy.",
